smc-full: take an empty block's checksum from the zero register

FEX-2609 turned the SMCChecks=full guard into a CRC32 over the guest bytes
of each instruction. an instruction FEXCore could not decode is emitted with
a CodeLength of 0, so no crc32 instruction is generated, but the result was
still read from TMP1 -- a scratch register only those instructions write.
whatever the dispatcher last left there reads as "the code changed": the
guard invalidates, exits to the same address, and the recompiled block does
the same again, forever. on a Snapdragon 8 Gen 3 this spun smc-full through
a whole Test Lab slot.

WorkingReg is TMP1 once any crc32 was emitted and the zero register when
none was, and the CRC of no bytes is 0 -- the compile-time value -- so the
guard of an empty block now passes, as it did under FEX-2608.

still present on FEX main as of 2026-10-07.

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp
@@ -401,7 +401,7 @@ DEF_OP(ValidateCode) {
     WorkingReg = TMP1;
   }
 
-  sub(ARMEmitter::Size::i32Bit, Dst, TMP1, CRC32Reg);
+  sub(ARMEmitter::Size::i32Bit, Dst, WorkingReg.W(), CRC32Reg);
 
   ARMEmitter::ForwardLabel End;
   cbz_OrRestart(ARMEmitter::Size::i32Bit, Dst, &End);
